  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 49a9dd75b14f64f43a98b9b523c7ac90, type: 3}
  m_Name: AlexCubicle
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueObject
  _concurrentDialogue:
  - I almost thought Alex would come in today. When I last saw her, she told me she
    had a really bad fight with her mom.
  - She was crying, saying that she never wanted to see her again. She hugged me
    that day.
  - That was the last contact I had with someone. The last contact I ever will have
    with someone.
  - "When I heard the news, I started to think there was a chance I would see her
    today. We could look out the window and reminisce about nothing. We wouldn\u2019t
    be alone."
  - But I guess she reconciled with her mom. The announcement of a nuclear war might
    have helped.
  - "I'd be really glad if she did. She won\u2019t have any regrets."
  - I know I certainly do.
  - "She\u2019ll have someone that loves her be with her on this last day."
  - I wish I could have reconciled with everyone.
  - Marcy especially, Dan, and Andrew as well.
  - 'I wish someone would watch the sunset out this window with me tonight.  '
  _characterName: You
  _nextDialogue: {fileID: 0}
  _choices: {fileID: 0}
